  "sources": [
    "Kansas City Chiefs, 'From a state-of-the-art scoreboard and new seats to updated infrastructure' (2019-08-27, chiefs.com) and Daktronics, 'Daktronics upgrades Arrowhead Stadium for Kansas City Chiefs': in 2019 the west end zone display was replaced with a 37 ft high by 150 ft wide HDR board (10 mm), with the GEHA Drum Deck (now the Drum Deck: the GEHA name ended on 2026-08-05) below it; the east end keeps its football-shaped display (the 2010 HD retrofit, Wikipedia).",
    "Which end is west (PROVED OFFLINE, retail against photo): the retail +z end carries the smaller oval with a small board on posts above it, as the east end does in the October 2019 Commons photo from section 335 behind the CHIEFS end zone (r007); so -z, with the larger oval, the flag and the two flanking boards, is the west end.",
    "The retail s13 scene (PROVED OFFLINE): the west oval is group379 (the 10.7 x 6.4 m feed, its frame, posts and flag in lite01, its back in wall01; the shape is removed) and group370's ad01 face at z -105.5 (cut); the flanking boards at x +-34 to +-51 stay. The west upper deck's centre section is one sloped seat quad under rows of crowd strips; its parapet (wall01, 2 m) runs z -107.73 at the centre to -105.49 at x +-28.66, its top 40.2 to 40.8 m.",
    "DESIGN: the board stands on the parapet at the centre (its face at z -107.9, its frame's foot at 40.2 m), on a concrete base behind the parapet with a cap from the parapet to the base, so it reads as mounted from the field and from the air; frame and body in the retail concrete (wall010) at a dark colour, since rail02 is a see-through railing. The Drum Deck is a concrete platform over the centre section's top three rows (their crowd strips cut), level with the parapet's foot (38.2 m), from z -102.9 to the parapet, with its front face down to the seats and a steel rail. The deck's name sign and the north-side World Cup seat removal are left out.",
    "DESIGN (main, 2026-09-29): a plain panel in the retail concrete at the board's dark colour covers the board's back (a solid panel from behind, the concrete's pattern tiled flat), 4 cm behind the body's back (z -109.54)."
  ],
  "team": "KC",
  "venue": "s13"
}
